<title>JAPAN: Swedish Export Credit launches 5.55% dual samurais.</title>
<headline>Swedish Export Credit launches 5.55% dual samurais.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-10-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Export Credit Corp (SEK) on Wednesday launched 50 billion yen worth of 5.55 percent yen/Australian dollar dual currency samurai bonds due on November 18, 1999, lead-manager Yamaichi Securities said.</p>
<p>The bonds are priced at par and the coupon payments will be made twice a year.  </p>
<p>The coupon will be paid in yen, while redemption will be in Australian dollars.</p>
<p>Holders of the samurai bonds will receive A$5,524.86 for each 500,000-yen bond held at maturity.</p>
</text>
